---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="klymot labs" description="Hands-on, interactive explorations of climate data.">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script>
      import { sendPageBeacon, sendFeatureBeacon } from '../lib/analytics.js';
      sendPageBeacon();
      sendFeatureBeacon('labs/index/01-visited');
    </script>
  </Fragment>

  <header class="site-header">
    <div class="container header-inner">
      <a class="brand-link" href="https://klymot.com" aria-label="klymot home">
        <span class="brand-logo" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" width="22" height="22">
            <circle cx="16" cy="16" r="13" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.25"/>
            <ellipse cx="16" cy="16" rx="13" ry="4.2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.8" opacity="0.5"/>
            <ellipse cx="16" cy="9.5" rx="10" ry="2.8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.8" opacity="0.5"/>
            <ellipse cx="16" cy="22.5" rx="10" ry="2.8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.8" opacity="0.5"/>
            <ellipse cx="16" cy="16" rx="3" ry="13" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.8" opacity="0.5"/>
            <ellipse cx="16" cy="16" rx="9" ry="13" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.8" opacity="0.5"/>
            <circle cx="19.5" cy="10.5" r="4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" fill="none" opacity="0.4"/>
            <circle cx="19.5" cy="10.5" r="2" fill="currentColor"/>
          </svg>
        </span>
        <span class="brand-title">klymot</span>
        <span class="brand-sub">· labs</span>
      </a>
      <button class="theme-toggle" id="themeToggle" aria-label="Toggle theme" type="button">◐</button>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main>
    <div class="container">

      <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="site-heading">
        <span class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true">Labs</span>
        <h1 id="site-heading">klymot labs</h1>
        <p class="lede">Hands-on explorations of climate data.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-label="Available labs">
        <div class="labs-grid">
          <a class="lab-card" href="./sunshine-temperature/">
            <span class="lab-number">Lab 01</span>
            <h2 class="lab-title">Sunshine &amp; Temperature</h2>
            <p class="lab-desc">Explore the relationship between incoming solar radiation and surface temperature using pyranometer recordings and GHCN station records.</p>
            <span class="lab-cta" aria-hidden="true">Open lab →</span>
          </a>
          <a class="lab-card" href="./network-altitude/">
            <span class="lab-number">Lab 02</span>
            <h2 class="lab-title">Network Altitude</h2>
            <p class="lab-desc">How has the shifting altitude profile of the global temperature station network changed over time? Follow the physics, then check.</p>
            <span class="lab-cta" aria-hidden="true">Open lab →</span>
          </a>
          <a class="lab-card" href="./cherry-picking/">
            <span class="lab-number">Lab 03</span>
            <h2 class="lab-title">The Cherry-Picking Machine</h2>
            <p class="lab-desc">Every quoted temperature trend rests on two choices: how many years, and which ones. Drag a window along a real station record, tally every trend you pass over, and see where the whole record lands in the distribution you built.</p>
            <span class="lab-cta" aria-hidden="true">Open lab →</span>
          </a>
          <a class="lab-card" href="./error-bars-sunshine/">
            <span class="lab-number">Lab 04</span>
            <h2 class="lab-title">Build Your Own Error Bars — Sunshine</h2>
            <p class="lab-desc">Where a pyranometer exists, sunshine is measured; everywhere else the number comes from a model. Put decades of real solar measurements next to the model's estimate for the same spot, build the distribution of their disagreements, freeze an error band around it — then test whether that band holds at a site it has never seen.</p>
            <span class="lab-cta" aria-hidden="true">Open lab →</span>
          </a>
          <a class="lab-card" href="./error-bars-temperature/">
            <span class="lab-number">Lab 05</span>
            <h2 class="lab-title">Build Your Own Error Bars — Temperature</h2>
            <p class="lab-desc">Weather archives hold two kinds of number for the same place and month: what a thermometer recorded, and what a weather model reconstructs. Put a station's own record next to the model's reconstruction for the same spot, build the distribution of their disagreements, freeze an error band around it — then test whether that band holds at a station it has never seen.</p>
            <span class="lab-cta" aria-hidden="true">Open lab →</span>
          </a>
          <a class="lab-card" href="./airless-body/">
            <span class="lab-number">Lab 06</span>
            <h2 class="lab-title">Airless Body Thermal Model</h2>
            <p class="lab-desc">How much of the Moon's temperature can sunlight, conduction, and radiation alone explain? Choose a conductivity model, set the parameters, run the simulation in your browser, and compare the result with NASA's measured lunar temperatures.</p>
            <span class="lab-cta" aria-hidden="true">Open lab →</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    <div class="container">
      <p>© Klymot</p>
    </div>
  </footer>
</BaseLayout>
